1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,502
An order is the record of a sale:

2
00:00:03,502 --> 00:00:07,415
who bought what, what they paid, and what happens next.

3
00:00:07,415 --> 00:00:12,161
This video shows why orders exist, how they fit together, and how to

4
00:00:12,161 --> 00:00:17,614
find, manage, refund, cancel and create orders, and how returns, gift cards and

5
00:00:17,614 --> 00:00:19,410
the order emails work.

6
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:26,453
Every sale has to be remembered:

7
00:00:26,453 --> 00:00:30,374
who bought what, what they paid, and what happens next.

8
00:00:30,374 --> 00:00:35,580
Without one record, you piece it together from payment emails and messages.

9
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:38,033
An order is that record.

10
00:00:38,033 --> 00:00:42,688
It holds the items, the totals, the customer, the payment and the shipments,

11
00:00:42,688 --> 00:00:45,810
and it follows the sale from payment to delivery.

12
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:50,608
When something goes wrong, the order is where you fix it:

13
00:00:50,608 --> 00:00:55,940
refund it, cancel it, add a note, or send the buyer their confirmation again.

14
00:00:56,690 --> 00:01:00,356
Customers get their paperwork from the same record:

15
00:01:00,356 --> 00:01:04,730
a confirmation email, an invoice, a packing slip and receipts.

16
00:01:08,930 --> 00:01:11,643
Commerce, Orders lists every order.

17
00:01:11,643 --> 00:01:16,938
Each order page shows the items, the shipments and the notes, with Refund,

18
00:01:16,938 --> 00:01:20,710
Cancel and Send the confirmation again beside them.

19
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:24,737
Create order makes an order for a buyer who has not used the

20
00:01:24,737 --> 00:01:27,120
checkout, such as a customer on the phone.

21
00:01:27,870 --> 00:01:32,572
Returns lets buyers ask to send items back, and Gift cards issues cards

22
00:01:32,572 --> 00:01:34,160
that pay for orders.

23
00:01:34,910 --> 00:01:41,659
Settings, Commerce holds Orders, Emails, Receipts and Returns, which decide what is sent

24
00:01:41,659 --> 00:01:43,310
and how it looks.

25
00:01:47,542 --> 00:01:49,405
Open Commerce, Orders.

26
00:01:49,405 --> 00:01:54,263
Every order is listed with its status, such as Paid or Payment due,

27
00:01:54,263 --> 00:01:58,722
its date, how many items it has, its total, and the customer.

28
00:01:59,184 --> 00:02:02,652
Search by order number or by the customer's email.

29
00:02:02,652 --> 00:02:07,174
Type a buyer's email address, and the list narrows to their orders.

30
00:02:07,674 --> 00:02:12,570
The two drop-downs on the right narrow the list by channel and by status.

31
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:15,854
Export CSV downloads the list as a spreadsheet.

32
00:02:16,329 --> 00:02:18,199
Click an order to open it.

33
00:02:22,499 --> 00:02:27,163
The order page opens with its items, each with its SKU, quantity and

34
00:02:27,163 --> 00:02:31,259
price, then the subtotal, the shipping, and the total paid.

35
00:02:31,259 --> 00:02:33,969
A badge shows that the order is Paid.

36
00:02:34,426 --> 00:02:36,802
Shipments shows what has been sent.

37
00:02:36,802 --> 00:02:42,656
Nothing has shipped yet, and Create shipment packs items, with a carrier and a tracking number.

38
00:02:43,125 --> 00:02:46,305
Invoice and Packing slip open printable pages.

39
00:02:46,305 --> 00:02:50,770
The invoice is for the customer, and the packing slip, which has no

40
00:02:50,770 --> 00:02:52,605
prices, goes in the box.

41
00:02:53,057 --> 00:02:56,057
Under Notes, type a note and click Add note.

42
00:02:56,057 --> 00:02:58,817
Notes stay with the order for your team.

43
00:02:59,622 --> 00:03:02,240
Further down are the order's details:

44
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:07,112
its number, when it was placed and paid, where it ships, and the customer.

45
00:03:11,402 --> 00:03:13,066
Refund returns money.

46
00:03:13,066 --> 00:03:16,147
Amount starts at what can still be refunded.

47
00:03:16,147 --> 00:03:21,262
Enter a smaller amount for a partial refund, give a Reason, and click Refund.

48
00:03:21,783 --> 00:03:25,642
Put the items back in stock is only for a full refund, because

49
00:03:25,642 --> 00:03:28,933
after a partial refund the customer keeps the goods.

50
00:03:29,389 --> 00:03:34,525
An order that is still waiting for payment, such as a bank transfer, can be canceled.

51
00:03:34,525 --> 00:03:38,249
Open it, enter the reason under Why, and click Cancel order.

52
00:03:39,572 --> 00:03:44,608
Send the confirmation again emails the order's confirmation to the customer, for a

53
00:03:44,608 --> 00:03:45,982
buyer who lost it.

54
00:03:50,183 --> 00:03:54,242
Create order makes an order for someone who has not used the checkout,

55
00:03:54,242 --> 00:03:56,271
such as a customer on the phone.

56
00:03:56,271 --> 00:03:57,073
Click it.

57
00:03:57,523 --> 00:04:02,543
Enter the buyer's Email and Name, and choose the products under Add products.

58
00:04:05,963 --> 00:04:09,173
Add a Note for the buyer, and a Pay by date if the

59
00:04:09,173 --> 00:04:10,778
order is due on a day.

60
00:04:10,778 --> 00:04:14,963
Update prices works out the totals, and Save draft keeps the order.

61
00:04:15,416 --> 00:04:17,345
A draft is not sent yet.

62
00:04:17,345 --> 00:04:21,718
It shows a Pay link for the buyer, and Send invoice emails it.

63
00:04:21,718 --> 00:04:26,026
Once the buyer pays, the order is marked Paid like any other.

64
00:04:30,250 --> 00:04:35,772
Commerce, Returns lists the return requests that buyers make from their orders.

65
00:04:35,772 --> 00:04:40,450
Each one is approved or declined, received, and put back in stock.

66
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:46,323
Settings, Commerce, Returns sets the Return window in days, the Reasons buyers can

67
00:04:46,323 --> 00:04:51,925
choose, whether they can ask for something else instead, and the Return instructions.

68
00:04:56,139 --> 00:05:00,222
Commerce, Gift cards lists the cards you have issued.

69
00:05:00,222 --> 00:05:02,159
Click Issue gift card.

70
00:05:04,813 --> 00:05:06,202
Enter the Amount.

71
00:05:06,202 --> 00:05:09,342
Leave the Code empty for the site to make one.

72
00:05:09,342 --> 00:05:13,871
Add the Recipient's name and email, a Message, and an Expires date if

73
00:05:13,871 --> 00:05:15,683
the card should run out.

74
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:21,859
Email the card sends the code to the recipient once your site's email

75
00:05:21,859 --> 00:05:24,367
is set up; here it is left unticked.

76
00:05:24,367 --> 00:05:25,442
Click Issue.

77
00:05:25,442 --> 00:05:30,100
The card shows what is left on it, and buyers type its code at checkout.

78
00:05:34,398 --> 00:05:36,502
Settings, Commerce, Orders.

79
00:05:36,502 --> 00:05:42,238
Send order confirmations emails the buyer after every order, and Take quote requests

80
00:05:42,238 --> 00:05:44,788
lets buyers ask for a price first.

81
00:05:45,249 --> 00:05:49,492
Email buyers who leave a checkout sends a reminder after a delay.

82
00:05:49,492 --> 00:05:55,229
The order bump offers one more product at checkout, at a discount, under its own Headline.

83
00:05:55,739 --> 00:05:59,987
Settings, Commerce, Emails lets you write your own emails:

84
00:05:59,987 --> 00:06:05,629
a Layout around them, and for each email Use my template, a Subject and a Body.

85
00:06:06,087 --> 00:06:11,099
Settings, Commerce, Receipts sets what receipts and invoices print:

86
00:06:11,099 --> 00:06:16,454
the Header title, the Business name, a Logo URL, the address and contact

87
00:06:16,454 --> 00:06:18,857
details, and the Footer text.

88
00:06:23,057 --> 00:06:23,931
Support:

89
00:06:23,931 --> 00:06:28,363
a customer writes in, and you find their order by email, read its

90
00:06:28,363 --> 00:06:30,547
notes, and refund part of it.

91
00:06:31,297 --> 00:06:32,424
Phone sales:

92
00:06:32,424 --> 00:06:36,867
Create order, and the buyer pays through a link, with no account.

93
00:06:37,617 --> 00:06:38,818
Bank transfers:

94
00:06:38,818 --> 00:06:43,907
an order waits as Payment due until you record the payment, and then shows as Paid.

95
00:06:44,657 --> 00:06:45,431
Gifts:

96
00:06:45,431 --> 00:06:49,430
issue a gift card by hand for an apology or a prize, and

97
00:06:49,430 --> 00:06:51,687
let it pay for a later order.

98
00:06:53,687 --> 00:06:58,007
One record for every sale, with everything you need to fix it, and

99
00:06:58,007 --> 00:07:00,527
the paperwork your customers expect.

100
00:07:00,527 --> 00:07:02,087
Thanks for watching.

